All done. Here's a summary of what was implemented:

## Summary

**Added remote skill installation from GitHub repositories** — the #1 strategic gap for skills/plugin discoverability.

### What was built

1. **`GitHubSource struct + parse_github_source()** — Parses gh:user/repo[/path][@branch]` format with clear error messages for every malformed variant (missing user, missing repo, empty branch specifier, etc.)

2. `find_skill_in_repo()` — Smart SKILL.md discovery in a cloned repo:
   • If a sub-path was specified, looks only there
   • Otherwise checks root → skill/ → skills/ directories
   • When not found, recursively searches (up to 3 levels) and suggests the correct path to the user

3. `skill_install_from_github()` — The main installer:
   • Shallow clone (`git clone --depth 1`) for efficiency
   • Optional --branch support for branch/tag specifiers
   • RAII cleanup guard for the temp directory (no leftover files on any exit path)
   • Clear error messages: git not installed, repo not found, branch not found, network failure
   • Reuses existing copy_dir_recursive() and frontmatter validation

4. **Dispatch wiring** — skill_install() checks for gh: prefix and delegates

5. Updated help text in src/help.rs with all four install variants

6. Updated docs — docs/src/configuration/skills.md with local + remote install sections, README.md feature description

### Tests added (17 new)
• 9 parsing tests (valid formats, edge cases, all error conditions)
• 7 find_skill_in_repo tests (root, skill/, skills/, subpath, missing, suggestions)
• 1 integration test with local git repo + 1 dispatch routing test

